# A tryN.py answers one question and is then worthless -- what it measured belongs in
# SUMMARY.md, which is committed. Keeping them out of history also avoids the trap
# unitree_rl_lab recorded: stale tries lingering in the tree, silently inheriting later
# edits to the configs they build on, and being re-run as if they still meant what they
# did. __init__.py registers whichever happen to exist, so a checkout without any is
# fine -- it just registers no sandbox tasks.
try*.py
ablation.py
